asr-000521
01:39:48.400 --> 01:39:49.580
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Chair hears none.

asr-000522
01:39:49.680 --> 01:39:57.200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Secretary General is hereby directed to read the titles of bills and resolutions on first reading as well as messages, communications, and committee reports.

asr-000523
01:39:57.200 --> 01:39:58.860
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Referral to the appropriate committees.

asr-000524
01:39:59.700 --> 01:40:07.060
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Madam Speaker, I had a pending parliamentary inquiry, so I would like to request the Majority Leader to reply to the parliamentary inquiry.

asr-000525
01:40:07.440 --> 01:40:09.740
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: May we know the parliamentary inquiry of the Honorable Chanko?

asr-000526
01:40:10.060 --> 01:40:19.840
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Ang tinanong ko po kanina is kung bakit po nilipat yung budget ng House of Representatives magpula po September 24 papunta pong September 17.

asr-000527
01:40:21.220 --> 01:40:26.840
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: As what the Majority Leader earlier responded, the adjustment involved the proposed budget.

asr-000528
01:40:27.200 --> 01:40:30.300
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The budget of the Department of Tourism and the Congress of the Philippines.

asr-000529
01:40:31.500 --> 01:40:35.380
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yes, Madam Speaker, alam ko po na hindi natuloy yung sa Department of Tourism.

asr-000530
01:40:35.640 --> 01:40:44.180
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kaya lang po, ang ginagawa po natin, kaya po tayo nagbibigay ng schedules ng budget is para po makapaghanda yung mga members na magtanong.

asr-000531
01:40:44.180 --> 01:40:55.680
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So kung ang budget ng House ay September 24 pa, natural po ang paghahandaan muna ay yung mga September 18, September 21.

asr-000532
01:40:57.200 --> 01:40:59.620
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So mas logical kung doon po humugot.

asr-000533
01:40:59.860 --> 01:41:03.340
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kaya lang, what was the compelling reason? Ano po yung napakahalaga?

asr-000534
01:41:04.200 --> 01:41:09.800
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Bakit inuna yung budget ng House of Representatives when traditionally nasa dulo po yan?

asr-000535
01:41:09.800 --> 01:41:20.160
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: As I was also the presiding during that week, distinguished colleague, the reason that the budget was adjusted was that two departments were also deferred.

asr-000536
01:41:20.580 --> 01:41:24.740
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: That is DICT and DEPDEV, specifically the Philippine Statistics Authority.

asr-000541
01:41:25.660 --> 01:41:33.920
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Hence, the adjustment of the other budgets to an earlier schedule, citing from the motion of the minority and the majority that there were no more interpellators.

asr-000542
01:41:34.940 --> 01:41:43.100
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: However, if the Hon. Changko is so much willing, we can inform the Committee on Appropriations that you be informed if in case there are other schedules.

asr-000543
01:41:44.060 --> 01:41:47.740
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Madam Speaker, may precedent na po tayo dito.

asr-000544
01:41:48.780 --> 01:41:52.560
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yung budget po ng MMDA, na-terminate po yun.

asr-000545
01:41:53.580 --> 01:41:56.460
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Tapos, the Hon. Tino requested that

asr-000546
01:41:56.460 --> 01:41:57.280
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: It be reopened.

asr-000547
01:41:57.960 --> 01:41:59.500
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: And pinayagan po siya to reopen.

asr-000548
01:42:00.340 --> 01:42:01.920
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So, I'm asking for the same thing.

asr-000549
01:42:02.200 --> 01:42:07.280
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Sa budget ng house, na sana po payagan na ma-reopen yung budget ng house.

asr-000550
01:42:07.520 --> 01:42:08.700
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: For the following reasons.

asr-000551
01:42:09.520 --> 01:42:20.440
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Number one, noong pa lang po DBCC, on the first day, nag-request na po ako na dalhin sa committee yung budget ng house.

asr-000552
01:42:21.140 --> 01:42:22.180
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Ngunit hindi po pumayag.

asr-000553
01:42:23.180 --> 01:42:24.980
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So, sa plenaryo na lang po.

asr-000554
01:42:25.660 --> 01:42:26.380
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Hindi po magandang tingin.

asr-000555
01:42:26.460 --> 01:42:33.340
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Hindi po magandang tignan na ang budget ng house, eh hindi man lang pinaliwanag dito sa plenaryo at pinasa natin.

asr-000556
01:42:33.720 --> 01:42:39.860
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kaya po, humihingi po ako ng reconsideration na since pinagbigyan po yung MMDA na ma-reopen,

asr-000557
01:42:40.400 --> 01:42:42.500
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: eh sana ma-reopen din po yung sa house.

asr-000558
01:42:42.900 --> 01:42:45.440
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: At tayo ay nasa isang unique na katayuan.

asr-000559
01:42:46.140 --> 01:42:51.620
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Tayo po ang ahensya at tayo po ang sangay ng gobyerno na may kapangyarihan sa budget.

asr-000560
01:42:51.620 --> 01:42:56.440
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Pero tayo lang rin ang sangay ng gobyerno na may control ng budget.

asr-000561
01:42:56.460 --> 01:42:58.360
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Na gumagastos ng sariling budget.

asr-000562
01:42:58.760 --> 01:43:03.900
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yung ibang ahensya po na pupunta dito, pumupunta sila dito sa Kongreso para humingi ng pondo.

asr-000563
01:43:04.760 --> 01:43:08.560
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Pero hindi po pareho yung nagbibigay at nagre-release ng pondo.

asr-000564
01:43:08.680 --> 01:43:12.700
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: With the indulgence of our distinguished colleague,

asr-000565
01:43:12.800 --> 01:43:15.120
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: we are still in the additional reference of business.

asr-000566
01:43:15.560 --> 01:43:17.460
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: What you are referring to is under unfinished business.

asr-000567
01:43:18.540 --> 01:43:21.180
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: We will go to that agenda that is third in our agenda.

asr-000568
01:43:21.660 --> 01:43:23.200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Secretary General is hereby directed.

asr-000569
01:43:23.200 --> 01:43:24.820
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay, so babalikan po natin yan after this.

asr-000570
01:43:24.820 --> 01:43:25.300
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Yes.

asr-000571
01:43:25.500 --> 01:43:25.800
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Okay.

asr-000572
01:43:25.800 --> 01:43:30.400
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Secretary General again is hereby directed to read the title of bills on first reading

asr-000573
01:43:30.400 --> 01:43:36.400
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: as well as committee reports resolution and for referral to the appropriate committee.

asr-000574
01:43:36.540 --> 01:43:37.000
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: So directed.

asr-000575
01:43:38.180 --> 01:43:39.940
Secretary-General: Additional reference of business.

asr-000576
01:43:40.500 --> 01:43:41.060
Secretary-General: Resolution.

asr-000577
01:43:41.620 --> 01:43:43.300
Secretary-General: House Resolution 1465.

asr-000578
01:43:44.000 --> 01:43:50.000
Secretary-General: Urging the DOE, the ERC, and the NGCP to fast-track, prioritize, and advance the timeline

asr-000579
01:43:50.000 --> 01:43:53.600
Secretary-General: for the early completion of the Mindoro-Panay Interconnection Project

asr-000580
01:43:53.600 --> 01:43:55.600
Secretary-General: to establish a power loop and ensure stability.

asr-000581
01:43:55.800 --> 01:43:58.500
Secretary-General: And to establish a stable energy for Panay Island and western Visayas.

asr-000582
01:43:58.940 --> 01:44:00.040
Secretary-General: Representative Baronda.

asr-000583
01:44:06.140 --> 01:44:08.920
Secretary-General: To the Committee on Energy.

asr-000584
01:44:09.880 --> 01:44:11.060
Secretary-General: Committee Reports.

asr-000585
01:44:11.280 --> 01:44:14.400
Secretary-General: Committee Report number 643, 644, and 645.

asr-000586
01:44:15.020 --> 01:44:17.120
Secretary-General: Submitted by the Committee on Youth and Sports Development

asr-000587
01:44:17.120 --> 01:44:20.980
Secretary-General: on House Resolution 1462, House Bill number 11380,

asr-000588
01:44:21.420 --> 01:44:23.760
Secretary-General: and House Resolution 1463, respectively.

asr-000589
01:44:25.800 --> 01:44:26.780
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: To the Committee on Rules.

asr-000590
01:44:28.160 --> 01:44:28.960
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

asr-000591
01:44:51.960 --> 01:44:53.720
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Suspend session for a few minutes.

asr-000592
01:44:54.780 --> 01:44:55.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Session suspended.

asr-000596
01:46:00.000 --> 01:46:29.980
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Session resumed. Majority Leader.

asr-000597
01:46:30.000 --> 01:46:48.440
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Madam Speaker, I move that we resume consideration of House Bill No. 10858.

asr-000597-split-2
01:46:48.440 --> 01:47:02.440
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: There's a motion to resume consideration of House Bill No. 10858 as contained in Committee Report No. 638, and the Secretary-General is hereby directed to read the title of said measure.

asr-000598
01:47:02.440 --> 01:47:19.760
Secretary-General: House Bill No. 10858, an act appropriating funds for the operation of the Government of the Republic of the Philippines from January 1 to December 31, 2027.

asr-000598-split-2
01:47:19.760 --> 01:47:25.960
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

asr-000598-split-3
01:47:25.960 --> 01:47:32.840
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Madam Speaker, I move to recognize the representative of the Lone District.

asr-000599
01:47:32.840 --> 01:47:37.240
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Toby Tiangco is hereby recognized. Please proceed.

asr-000599-split-2
01:47:37.240 --> 01:47:57.600
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Madam Speaker, papagpatuloy ko lang po. Inusod po yung schedule ng [unclear] po ay pinayagan po ma-reopen para makapagtanong. Dito po sa House, nagre-request po ako ng reopening. Hindi naman po siguro maganda na wala akong nakapagtanong dito sa budget ng House.

asr-000599-split-3
01:47:57.600 --> 01:47:58.640
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Is it a motion?

asr-000599-split-4
01:47:58.640 --> 01:48:00.960
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yes, patapusin lang po.

asr-000600
01:48:00.960 --> 01:48:29.980
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Considering po na sa lahat ng sangay ng gobyerno, tayo po ay allowed ng liquidation by certification. So kung allowed po tayo ng liquidation by certification, mas lalong dapat ipaliwanag sa taong bayan papaano po ginagastos yung pera nila dahil hindi naman po natin ito [unclear]. So I'm asking for a motion for reconsideration to reopen the budget of the House and be presented to the plenary in the same way that it was allowed for the MMDA.

asr-000601
01:48:30.000 --> 01:48:33.080
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: With the indulgence of our distinguished colleague,

asr-000602
01:48:33.800 --> 01:48:39.000
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: while the proposed budget of the MMDA was indeed reconsidered

asr-000603
01:48:39.620 --> 01:48:43.660
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: upon the motion of the majority giving way and yielding way

asr-000604
01:48:43.660 --> 01:48:47.880
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: to the listed members who arrived and who wished their intention to interpolate,

asr-000605
01:48:49.180 --> 01:48:52.080
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: in the case of the budget of the House of Representatives,

asr-000606
01:48:53.160 --> 01:48:57.320
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: it does not mean that the leadership doesn't want to discuss the proposed budget.

asr-000607
01:48:57.320 --> 01:48:58.040
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: In fact,

asr-000608
01:48:58.860 --> 01:48:59.820
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: the House is very much...

asr-000609
01:49:00.000 --> 01:49:01.660
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: very much willing to discuss this.

asr-000610
01:49:02.360 --> 01:49:02.780
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: However,

asr-000611
01:49:03.420 --> 01:49:04.060
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: if I may,

asr-000612
01:49:04.440 --> 01:49:07.420
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and with respectful indulgence to our distinguished colleague,

asr-000613
01:49:08.060 --> 01:49:10.840
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Section 105 of our rules states,

asr-000614
01:49:11.540 --> 01:49:14.800
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: when a measure, report, or motion is approved, adopted, or lost,

asr-000615
01:49:15.200 --> 01:49:19.160
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: a member who voted with the majority may move for its reconsideration on the same

asr-000616
01:49:19.160 --> 01:49:21.180
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: or succeeding session day.

asr-000617
01:49:21.780 --> 01:49:24.040
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: As we have conferred with the Secretary General,

asr-000618
01:49:24.660 --> 01:49:27.300
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: the Honorable Toby Chanko was on official business,

asr-000619
01:49:27.300 --> 01:49:29.580
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: on official travel abroad,

asr-000620
01:49:30.000 --> 01:49:33.740
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: hence, with due courtesy, Honorable Toby Chanko,

asr-000621
01:49:34.880 --> 01:49:37.640
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: your motion for reconsideration is out of order.

asr-000622
01:49:37.640 --> 01:49:40.840
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: No, Madam Speaker, it says on the next session day.

asr-000623
01:49:41.340 --> 01:49:44.460
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: We are not yet on the next session day because we have not yet adjourned.

asr-000624
01:49:44.460 --> 01:49:47.800
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So we are still in the same session day, Madam Speaker.

asr-000625
01:49:47.800 --> 01:49:50.160
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So you cannot use that rule, Madam Speaker.

asr-000626
01:49:50.160 --> 01:49:52.760
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: It says on the next session day.

asr-000627
01:49:52.760 --> 01:49:55.320
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: We are still on the same session day, so it's a continuing session.

asr-000628
01:49:55.320 --> 01:49:59.680
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So dapat po kung ganyan ang gusto niyong gamitin na rule, dapat po

asr-000629
01:49:59.680 --> 01:50:07.240
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: nag-adjourn po noon para next session day, eh Biyernes at hindi na po ako puwedeng mag-motion for reconsideration ngayon.

asr-000630
01:50:07.340 --> 01:50:09.680
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: I am not actually referring to the next session day.

asr-000631
01:50:09.980 --> 01:50:15.620
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: I am referring, the presiding officer, referring to a motion for reconsideration of a member

asr-000632
01:50:15.620 --> 01:50:19.620
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: who voted with the majority insofar as the motion

asr-000633
01:50:19.620 --> 01:50:24.860
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: to terminate the period of interpolation of the proposed budget of the Congress of the Philippines.

asr-000634
01:50:24.860 --> 01:50:26.200
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Within the next session day.

asr-000635
01:50:26.960 --> 01:50:29.480
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Hindi pa po tumadaan yung isang session day, Madam Speaker.

asr-000636
01:50:29.500 --> 01:50:29.680
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Yes.

asr-000637
01:50:29.840 --> 01:50:31.880
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Anyway, just rule on it, Madam Speaker.

asr-000638
01:50:32.000 --> 01:50:34.740
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kung talagang hindi kayo papayag, then just rule on it.

asr-000639
01:50:35.000 --> 01:50:36.860
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The parliamentary status is this.

asr-000640
01:50:37.500 --> 01:50:41.820
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The proposed, the interpolations of the proposed budget of the House of Representatives

asr-000641
01:50:41.820 --> 01:50:45.060
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: has been terminated as moved by the minority,

asr-000642
01:50:45.240 --> 01:50:49.820
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: duly seconded by the majority last Thursday, September...

asr-000643
01:50:53.480 --> 01:50:57.820
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: September 17, 2026 at approximately...

asr-000644
01:50:59.840 --> 01:51:00.900
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: before noontime.

asr-000645
01:51:01.820 --> 01:51:05.860
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: A motion for reconsideration is being put forwarded by the Honorable Chanko.

asr-000646
01:51:06.420 --> 01:51:09.580
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: While the presiding officer would gladly yield,

asr-000647
01:51:10.100 --> 01:51:14.760
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: unfortunately, our rule states that only a member who had voted with the majority

asr-000648
01:51:14.760 --> 01:51:17.220
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: can vote for the reconsideration.

asr-000649
01:51:17.380 --> 01:51:19.200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: With that, our apologies.

asr-000650
01:51:19.920 --> 01:51:22.200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The motion for reconsideration is out of order.

asr-000651
01:51:22.460 --> 01:51:22.840
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: So ruled.

asr-000652
01:51:23.600 --> 01:51:24.420
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-000653
01:51:24.420 --> 01:51:28.840
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: But I think more than the rules, transparency is more important than our rules.

asr-000654
01:51:28.960 --> 01:51:29.820
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kasi kung gusto po natin,

asr-000655
01:51:29.840 --> 01:51:31.460
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: magigilan ng korupsyon,

asr-000656
01:51:32.160 --> 01:51:33.360
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: kailangan po may accountability.

asr-000657
01:51:33.880 --> 01:51:36.600
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kung wala pong accountability, kung wala pong transparency.

asr-000658
01:51:37.200 --> 01:51:39.900
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So, but if that is your rule, then I will respect it.

asr-000659
01:51:42.240 --> 01:51:44.140
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Thank you very much, Honorable Chanko.

asr-000660
01:51:44.200 --> 01:51:44.840
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader?

asr-000661
01:51:50.820 --> 01:51:54.660
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Madam Speaker, I move to consider the proposed budget of the Commission on Audit.

asr-000662
01:51:57.060 --> 01:51:58.540
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: There's a motion to

asr-000663
01:51:58.540 --> 01:52:02.320
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: consider the proposed budget of the Commission on Audit.

asr-000665
01:52:03.860 --> 01:52:04.840
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: An objection?

asr-000666
01:52:05.540 --> 01:52:11.380
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Hearing none, the period of sponsorship debate and interpolation on the proposed budget of the Commission on Audit is hereby opened.

asr-000667
01:52:11.880 --> 01:52:12.760
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader?

asr-000668
01:52:13.240 --> 01:52:17.140
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Madam Speaker, may we acknowledge the heads and officials of the Commission on Audit,

asr-000669
01:52:17.300 --> 01:52:17.640
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: namely,

asr-000670
01:52:17.920 --> 01:52:19.780
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Chairperson Gamaliel Cordoba,

asr-000671
01:52:20.600 --> 01:52:23.500
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Commissioner Douglas Michael Malilin,

asr-000672
01:52:24.680 --> 01:52:27.280
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Assistant Commissioner Alexander Juliano,

asr-000673
01:52:27.280 --> 01:52:29.180
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Assistant Commissioner Nilda Plaver,

asr-000674
01:52:29.820 --> 01:52:57.540
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Assistant Commissioner Martha Roxana Cese, Assistant Commissioner Lorna Cabotchan, Assistant Commissioner Roy Ursal, Assistant Commissioner Joel Estolatan, Assistant Commissioner Lito Martin, Assistant Commissioner Bresilo Sabaldan, Assistant Commissioner Lucila Isidro, Assistant Commissioner Sofia Hemora, and Assistant Commissioner Estela Mercado.

asr-000675
01:52:59.820 --> 01:53:14.200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Commission on Audit family, headed by the Chairperson, Gamaliel Cordoba, who never ages except for the missing few strands of hair.

asr-000676
01:53:14.800 --> 01:53:19.540
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Maraming salamat sa pagdalo dito sa Kongreso kasama ang COA family.

asr-000677
01:53:19.880 --> 01:53:20.620
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

asr-000678
01:53:22.060 --> 01:53:25.680
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Madam Speaker, I move that we open the period of sponsorship and debate.

asr-000679
01:53:29.820 --> 01:53:41.440
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: I move that we recognize the Honorable Vice Chairperson, the Honorable John Tracy Cagas, of the Lone District of Davao del Sur, to sponsor the proposed budget of the Commission on Audit.

asr-000680
01:53:41.940 --> 01:53:50.880
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Vice Chairperson, John Tracy Cagas, of the Lone District of Davao del Sur, is hereby recognized to sponsor the proposed budget of the Commission on Audit.

asr-000681
01:53:51.500 --> 01:53:53.480
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000682
01:53:55.260 --> 01:53:59.440
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: I would like also to include or acknowledge the respective

asr-000683
01:53:59.820 --> 01:54:07.480
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Regional Directors of COA, from the different regions of our beloved country.

asr-000684
01:54:09.740 --> 01:54:17.520
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleagues, magandang hapon po sa ating lahat.

asr-000685
01:54:17.520 --> 01:54:26.520
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: It is my honor to sponsor the budget of the Commission on Audit for Fiscal Year 2027,

asr-000686
01:54:28.140 --> 01:54:29.520
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: amounting to

asr-000687
01:54:29.820 --> 01:54:37.040
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: 16.46 billion pesos, inclusive of the automatic appropriations.

asr-000688
01:54:38.040 --> 01:54:45.020
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: In terms of new appropriations, which is subject for Congressional approval,

asr-000689
01:54:46.540 --> 01:54:52.460
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: the total budget of COA amounts to 14.774 billion,

asr-000690
01:54:52.460 --> 01:54:58.460
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: which represents an increase of about 2.49%.

asr-000691
01:54:59.820 --> 01:55:12.000
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: or 359.12 million, higher than the Fiscal Year 2026 level of 14.415 billion.

asr-000692
01:55:13.220 --> 01:55:22.720
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Madam Speaker, this budget will be used to support the Commission's program, activities, and operations,

asr-000693
01:55:22.720 --> 01:55:26.720
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: to ensure accountability for public resources,

asr-000694
01:55:28.260 --> 01:55:29.660
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: promote transparency,

asr-000695
01:55:29.840 --> 01:55:32.760
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: and help improve government operations

asr-000696
01:55:33.540 --> 01:55:39.400
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: in partnership with stakeholders for the benefit of the Filipino people.

asr-000697
01:55:40.480 --> 01:55:46.620
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: The Commission on Audit is the supreme auditing institution of our nation.

asr-000698
01:55:47.740 --> 01:55:51.900
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: It is the ultimate guardian for the public treasury

asr-000699
01:55:51.900 --> 01:55:56.200
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: and the bedrock of fiscal accountability.

asr-000701
01:55:56.240 --> 01:56:20.640
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: COA does not merely look at numbers. It ensures that every single peso contributed by our hardworking taxpayers is spent efficiently, effectively, and entirely for its intended public purpose.

asr-000702
01:56:20.640 --> 01:56:27.720
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: The proposed budget is a vital investment in good governance.

asr-000703
01:56:27.720 --> 01:56:43.760
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: By equipping COA with necessary resources, we are strengthening its capability to conduct rigorous audits, expand its workforce of dedicated state auditors,

asr-000704
01:56:43.760 --> 01:56:50.260
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: and adopt digital innovations that bring greater transparency.

asr-000705
01:56:50.640 --> 01:57:03.080
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: To starve COA of resources is to weaken our defenses against waste and corruption.

asr-000706
01:57:04.420 --> 01:57:11.040
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: To support COA is to fortify the integrity of our entire bureaucracy.

asr-000707
01:57:11.420 --> 01:57:17.940
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: As we steer our nation toward broader economic growth and development,

asr-000708
01:57:18.680 --> 01:57:20.620
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: let us ensure that our

asr-000710
01:57:20.640 --> 01:57:28.180
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: oversight institutions remain strong, independent, and fully capable.

asr-000711
01:57:29.240 --> 01:57:30.780
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000712
01:57:31.820 --> 01:57:39.660
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: This presentation is now ready to answer questions from our distinguished colleagues.

asr-000713
01:57:40.960 --> 01:57:42.200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

asr-000714
01:57:42.920 --> 01:57:49.280
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Iris Montes of the Partylist 4K

asr-000715
01:57:49.280 --> 01:57:50.380
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: to interpellate.

asr-000716
01:57:50.640 --> 01:57:52.860
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: On the proposed budget of the COA.

asr-000717
01:57:53.540 --> 01:57:57.580
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Honorable Iris Marie de Mesa Montes is hereby recognized for her interpellation.

asr-000718
01:57:58.360 --> 01:57:59.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000719
01:58:00.140 --> 01:58:02.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Magandang hapon po sa lahat.

asr-000720
01:58:02.380 --> 01:58:03.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ilang katanungan lamang po.

asr-000721
01:58:05.240 --> 01:58:09.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Unang tanong ko po, sa laki ng mandato ng COA,

asr-000722
01:58:10.040 --> 01:58:20.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sapat ba ang budget nito para maisa katuparan ang mas malawak at mas mabilis na auditing laban sa korupsyon?

asr-000723
01:58:20.640 --> 01:58:26.560
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: The question is, sapat na ba ang budget ng COA as proposed?

asr-000724
01:58:27.320 --> 01:58:32.880
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: The COA proposed originally before the NEP,

asr-000725
01:58:36.880 --> 01:58:41.580
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: 17 billion pesos.

asr-000726
01:58:41.580 --> 01:58:50.580
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Pero ang na-approve sa NEP ay 15 billion only.

asr-000727
01:58:50.640 --> 01:58:59.640
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yung dalawang bilyon na pesos ay para sana yun sa technological innovations.

asr-000728
01:59:00.140 --> 01:59:05.380
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Mga panibagong paggawa ng mga audit.

asr-000729
01:59:06.700 --> 01:59:16.660
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Unfortunately, we failed to provide what is necessary sa pamaraan ng pag-audit ngayon.

asr-000730
01:59:17.560 --> 01:59:18.740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000731
01:59:18.740 --> 01:59:20.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yan po kasi yung sunod kong isa.

asr-000732
01:59:20.640 --> 01:59:25.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Itatanong, doon sa kakulangan sa budget na trinopose po ng COA,

asr-000733
01:59:25.840 --> 01:59:28.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ano po ang mga proyekto o programang matatamaan?

asr-000734
01:59:29.500 --> 01:59:32.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At ang susunod ko pong katanungan sana,

asr-000735
01:59:32.800 --> 01:59:38.760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: magkano sana ang nakalaan sa proposed 2027 budget na dedicated to

asr-000736
01:59:38.760 --> 01:59:46.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: digital audit capabilities, data analytics, artificial intelligence, cyber security,

asr-000737
01:59:46.620 --> 01:59:50.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and automated detection of anomalous transactions?

asr-000738
01:59:50.640 --> 01:59:59.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kasi po, sa panahon ngayon, alam din po yan ng COA kung gaano kahalaga ang teknolohiyang ito para mas mapabilis.

asr-000739
01:59:59.500 --> 02:00:00.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: at

asr-000740
02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:04.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At mas accurate po yung ating mga audit reports.

asr-000741
02:00:11.240 --> 02:00:18.940
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: To be specific, distinguished interpellator, ito po yung nabawas, natanggal.

asr-000742
02:00:18.940 --> 02:00:36.060
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: M-O-O-E para sana sa mga P254 million and P420 pesos.

asr-000743
02:00:36.060 --> 02:00:51.300
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: At saka capital outlay na P1.177 million.

asr-000744
02:00:51.300 --> 02:00:52.100
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: 1 billion,

asr-000745
02:00:52.100 --> 02:00:54.580
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: 177 million.

asr-000746
02:00:55.560 --> 02:01:02.180
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: So, ang budget ng kuha ngayon, walang capital outlay.

asr-000747
02:01:07.880 --> 02:01:11.040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kung wala pong capital outlay, Mr. Speaker,

asr-000748
02:01:11.200 --> 02:01:15.420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ibig sabihin, hindi nga po tayo pwedeng mag-procure

asr-000749
02:01:15.420 --> 02:01:17.920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ng mga technological, ano,

asr-000750
02:01:18.940 --> 02:01:23.480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: equipment na makakatulong sana sa pag-audit ng kuha.

asr-000751
02:01:23.580 --> 02:01:24.300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, wala po.

asr-000752
02:01:24.680 --> 02:01:28.060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ibig sabihin po ba sa 2027 proposed budget,

asr-000753
02:01:28.380 --> 02:01:31.440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kahit SINGCO, wala pong nakalaan para doon?

asr-000754
02:01:35.520 --> 02:01:42.520
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: To be a specific, Madam Interpellator, distinguished interpellator,

asr-000755
02:01:43.360 --> 02:01:48.440
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: semi-expendable information and communication technology, ICT,

asr-000756
02:01:48.940 --> 02:01:52.340
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: ITEMS and software subscription,

asr-000757
02:01:53.320 --> 02:01:55.900
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: fiscal year 2027,

asr-000758
02:01:56.500 --> 02:02:03.400
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Kuha Information System Strategic Plan or ISSP,

asr-000759
02:02:04.140 --> 02:02:10.300
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: na umabot po ng P213,686,000.

asr-000760
02:02:10.300 --> 02:02:17.600
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: At saka yung Citizen Participatory Audit or CPA,

asr-000761
02:02:18.940 --> 02:02:24.160
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: MOOE requirements, yung mga NGOs, POs na sasali sana sa auditing,

asr-000762
02:02:24.460 --> 02:02:35.720
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: 40,734,000. Total po, 244?254 million 120,000.

asr-000763
02:02:35.720 --> 02:02:40.000
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Ito po sana yung gamitin para sa MOE, you know?

asr-000764
02:02:42.740 --> 02:02:47.360
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: At saka yung capital outlay naman, yung sa building ng kuha,

asr-000765
02:02:47.360 --> 02:02:54.320
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: building and structures, 484,617,000,

asr-000766
02:02:55.060 --> 02:03:01.820
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: yung mga furnitures and fixtures, 161,523,000,

asr-000767
02:03:02.540 --> 02:03:07.280
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: transportation equipment outlay, 5,600,000,

asr-000768
02:03:08.100 --> 02:03:15.460
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: ICT equipment and software, 525,405,000.

asr-000769
02:03:16.260 --> 02:03:17.300
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Total po.

asr-000770
02:03:17.360 --> 02:03:24.060
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Ang capital outlay is 1,177,145,000.

asr-000771
02:03:25.060 --> 02:03:28.760
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: So hindi na po na-consider sa NEP.

asr-000772
02:03:29.500 --> 02:03:35.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So ibig sabihin nga po, wala tayong gagamitin na pag-procure nitong mga ito?

asr-000773
02:03:36.760 --> 02:03:37.780
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Wala po, madam.

asr-000774
02:03:37.900 --> 02:03:43.680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So ibig sabihin din po niyan, since wala tayong budget para dyan,

asr-000775
02:03:43.680 --> 02:03:47.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: maaantala po sana yung isang,

asr-000776
02:03:47.360 --> 02:03:53.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: teknolohiyang pwede nating magamit para mas mapalakas at mapabilis ang ating audit.

asr-000777
02:03:53.480 --> 02:03:54.160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tama po ba?

asr-000778
02:03:55.060 --> 02:04:04.420
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yes, maaantala po yung trabaho nila sa mga bagong panibagong paraan sana.

asr-000779
02:04:05.020 --> 02:04:09.280
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Pero despite of it, I commend COA, you know?

asr-000780
02:04:11.280 --> 02:04:17.320
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Kung natatandaan natin, even the meager resources we are giving them,

asr-000781
02:04:17.360 --> 02:04:20.960
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: kahit kunti, they try their best.

asr-000782
02:04:21.960 --> 02:04:23.460
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Talagang nagsusumikap sila.

asr-000783
02:04:24.500 --> 02:04:29.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes, we acknowledge that, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague.

asr-000784
02:04:30.260 --> 02:04:34.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Pero syempre, gusto natin na bigyan din yung kahalagahan ng teknolohiya.

asr-000785
02:04:35.060 --> 02:04:41.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sa panahon ngayon na iba na po ang nakasanayan ng mga tao,

asr-000786
02:04:41.000 --> 02:04:47.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: o madami na pong pagbabago, dapat po syempre yung ating audit systems can keep up.

asr-000787
02:04:47.360 --> 02:04:50.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: With the changes na nangyayari din, ano po?

asr-000788
02:04:50.860 --> 02:04:57.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So yun lamang po ang gusto kong puntuhin na mahalaga na nababadgetan po natin yung teknolohiya

asr-000789
02:04:57.560 --> 02:04:59.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: para mas mapalakas po.

asr-000790
02:04:59.200 --> 02:05:06.580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Mamaya po, babanggitin ko po uli kung bakit mahalaga din po yung mga teknolohiyang yan.

asr-000791
02:05:06.900 --> 02:05:09.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: On to my next question, Madam Speaker.

asr-000792
02:05:09.700 --> 02:05:13.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Pagdating naman po sa coverage at sa capacity ng COA pa,

asr-000793
02:05:13.520 --> 02:05:16.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ilang porsyento ng mga ehensya at LG,

asr-000794
02:05:16.340 --> 02:05:19.200
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung aktwal na naa-audit ng COA kada taon.

asr-000795
02:05:19.940 --> 02:05:25.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Are we 100% naaabot po natin, isang daang porsyentong audit?

asr-000796
02:05:30.080 --> 02:05:36.620
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Except barangay, mga barangay local government units,

asr-000797
02:05:36.620 --> 02:05:45.520
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: lahat po ng munisipyo, probinsya, at national agencies ay na-audit po ng COA.

asr-000798
02:05:46.340 --> 02:05:49.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kung sakali po bang meron tayong technical capacity,

asr-000799
02:05:49.420 --> 02:05:52.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: maaabot po ba natin up to the barangay level?

asr-000800
02:05:52.240 --> 02:05:54.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: If our, you know, if our...

asr-000801
02:05:56.520 --> 02:05:59.680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano po ba ang dahilan kung bakit hindi naaabot yun?

asr-000802
02:05:59.800 --> 02:06:02.740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kulang sa oras? Kulang sa resources?

asr-000803
02:06:13.020 --> 02:06:15.360
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Ah, magandang tanong po yan.

asr-000804
02:06:15.780 --> 02:06:16.260
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Maganda.

asr-000805
02:06:17.000 --> 02:06:19.660
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: English Interpolator.

asr-000806
02:06:20.180 --> 02:06:23.700
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Kung merong sapat na teknolohiya.

asr-000807
02:06:24.880 --> 02:06:30.220
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Kasi ngayon, cyclical ay yung audit ng barangay every three years lang.

asr-000808
02:06:30.720 --> 02:06:33.600
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Sa dami, 42,000 barangays.

asr-000809
02:06:34.380 --> 02:06:37.240
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Pero kung may sapat na teknolohiya,

asr-000810
02:06:37.240 --> 02:06:44.100
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: pwede pong gawin yearly yung audit ng barangay.

asr-000811
02:06:44.680 --> 02:06:45.980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000812
02:06:46.340 --> 02:07:03.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Madam Speaker, pagdating naman po sa competence and integrity ng personal, paano po tinitiyak ng COA na ang kanilang mga auditors ay may sapat na training, competence at integridad upang hindi maging bahagi po ng problema?

asr-000813
02:07:03.880 --> 02:07:28.760
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yung tungkol po sa training, competency and capability of state auditors, upon entry po, pagpasok ng empleyado sa COA, start the training right away.

asr-000814
02:07:28.760 --> 02:07:32.340
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: At saka tuloy-tuloy na yan, hanggang tataas-tataas yan.

asr-000815
02:07:32.340 --> 02:07:52.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: We retain them in the agency. After training po ba, may porsyento po ba dyan na umaalis? O meron po silang, kumbaga may return service or kung meron hindi po return service, may pinirmahan na kontrata na magsiserve sila ng specific period?

asr-000816
02:08:02.340 --> 02:08:16.140
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yung mga specialized klase ng training, may kontrata po yun na they have to return the investment ng goberno.

asr-000817
02:08:17.040 --> 02:08:27.020
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Pero yung mga regular trainings, which is done regularly, wala naman pong kontrata yun. Yung mga specialized training lang po.

asr-000818
02:08:28.500 --> 02:08:32.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Do we also have, kaugnay po niyan, may budget po ba?

asr-000819
02:08:32.340 --> 02:08:55.420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Do we also have, na nakalaan sa pag-hire halimbawa ng mga engineers, yung mga IT specialists, yung mga specialized po na profession that can help COA detect mga highly technical din po na mga dapat na i-audit nila?

asr-000820
02:09:00.460 --> 02:09:02.320
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Gusto [unclear] ng COA

asr-000821
02:09:02.340 --> 02:09:17.340
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: na mag-hire ng mga specialized fields of knowledge. Limitado po yung item or plantilia ng COA. Meron silang engineer pero limited talaga.

asr-000822
02:09:18.060 --> 02:09:32.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes po. Thank you Madam Chair, Madam Speaker. Ang punto ko po kasi, alam naman natin kung how the government processes have become increasingly complex.

asr-000823
02:09:32.340 --> 02:09:59.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: complex sa panahon ngayon. And dagdag re-require din po ito na matugunan natin ng personnel who have the expertise. Halimbawa sa mga infrastructure projects, meron po ba tayo dyan sapat na mga ingeniero, arkitekto, siguro kasama pa yung mga financial analysts, tama po ba ang presyong ito?

asr-000824
02:09:59.560 --> 02:10:15.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kasi ako po naniniwala kung sapat po yung ating personnel, ang know-how ng ating personnel, ang kanilang experience, ang kanilang expertise, mabilis tayong gumawa, may teknolohiya tayo, mas mabilis po nating magagawa ang audit.

asr-000825
02:10:15.780 --> 02:10:28.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So ang tanong ko po sa COA, through the years, alam nyo po ito, ang sagot nyo po, wala kayong enough personnel, nag-request na po ba tayo sa DBM ng additional plantilia items?

asr-000826
02:10:28.900 --> 02:10:32.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Para matugunan natin ang gap na pong ito?

asr-000827
02:10:33.660 --> 02:10:41.140
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: The COA family fully agrees with you, Madam Interpellator.

asr-000828
02:10:44.580 --> 02:10:50.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Have you requested the DBM about the plantilia items that you need?

asr-000829
02:10:54.860 --> 02:10:58.860
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yes, the COA requested the DBM about the...

asr-000830
02:10:58.900 --> 02:11:02.040
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: plantilia items.

asr-000831
02:11:05.660 --> 02:11:08.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po, madam speaker.

asr-000832
02:11:09.460 --> 02:11:21.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Pagdating naman po sa effectiveness natin, ilang corruption-related audit findings nag-resulta po sa aktual na kaso o sanction noong 2025 na lamang po?

asr-000834
02:11:43.300 --> 02:11:45.800
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Thank you for asking that, madam tripulator.

asr-000835
02:11:47.740 --> 02:11:53.440
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Because that really ring a bell to our nation.

asr-000836
02:11:55.440 --> 02:12:03.100
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yung ginawa ng COA, arising from that scandal,

asr-000862
02:12:04.580 --> 02:12:07.540
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Nagpile ng COA ng fraud audit.

asr-000863
02:12:07.860 --> 02:12:09.240
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Nagawa ng fraud audit.

asr-000864
02:12:09.680 --> 02:12:19.300
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: At itong audit nila, yun ang ginawang basis or basihan para ma-file yun sa Ombudsman.

asr-000865
02:12:20.240 --> 02:12:24.840
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: So, more or less, about...

asr-000868
02:12:28.900 --> 02:12:45.860
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Bulacan alone, the epicenter of the, Bulacan alone, mga 50 cases, criminal cases, ang na-submit sa Ombudsman.

asr-000869
02:12:48.040 --> 02:12:50.160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000870
02:12:53.160 --> 02:12:58.320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Paano po nasisiguran ng COA na ang mga audit reports na ginagawa nito?

asr-000871
02:12:58.900 --> 02:13:04.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ay ano po ang sukatan na ginagamit na talagang nakakapagbawas tayo ng corruption sa gobyerno?

asr-000872
02:13:05.140 --> 02:13:06.680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: May sukatan po ba ang COA?

asr-000873
02:13:07.020 --> 02:13:11.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: How do you say that COA has been effective in decreasing corruption?

asr-000874
02:13:11.840 --> 02:13:14.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Anong metrics po ang ginagamit natin?

asr-000875
02:13:26.320 --> 02:13:27.720
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yung, ah,

asr-000876
02:13:28.220 --> 02:13:28.880
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: from the first,

asr-000877
02:13:28.900 --> 02:13:34.240
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: first step of COA's, ah, how do you call it, auditing process.

asr-000878
02:13:35.180 --> 02:13:37.160
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Isang ahensya po, ah,

asr-000879
02:13:37.940 --> 02:13:39.800
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: upon COA's knowledge, ah,

asr-000880
02:13:41.020 --> 02:13:41.780
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: merong, ano,

asr-000881
02:13:42.140 --> 02:13:47.060
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: something's not right, so,

asr-000882
02:13:47.700 --> 02:13:50.340
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: gawan po na rin, ano yan, ah,

asr-000883
02:13:51.180 --> 02:13:55.000
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: audit, EOM, audit observation memorandum.

asr-000884
02:13:55.800 --> 02:13:56.120
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: So,

asr-000885
02:13:56.120 --> 02:13:58.500
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: the agency concerned,

asr-000886
02:13:58.900 --> 02:14:00.900
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: kapat, ano siya, ah,

asr-000887
02:14:00.900 --> 02:14:04.900
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: he has to reply or respond to the EOM.

asr-000888
02:14:05.900 --> 02:14:11.900
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Pag ano, ah, na-satisfactory yung ano nila, ah, answer or respond,

asr-000889
02:14:11.900 --> 02:14:13.900
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: issue na po ng notice of

asr-000890
02:14:14.900 --> 02:14:16.900
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: disallowance, no?

asr-000891
02:14:16.900 --> 02:14:19.900
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Itong transaction na ito is disallowed.

asr-000892
02:14:19.900 --> 02:14:24.900
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Tapos, after notice of disallowance, ah,

asr-000893
02:14:28.900 --> 02:14:36.900
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: yung, ah,

asr-000894
02:14:36.900 --> 02:14:48.900
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: if he cannot answer, ah, yung notice of disallowance, ah, so, yun, ah, papuntang ombudsman na yung, ano.

asr-000895
02:14:48.900 --> 02:14:50.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000896
02:14:50.900 --> 02:14:57.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ahm, kasi halimbawa po may mga pagkakataon na discovery ng COA, isang malaking, ah, ah,

asr-000897
02:14:57.900 --> 02:14:59.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: um, anomalya.

asr-000898
02:15:00.000 --> 02:15:10.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Halimbawa po, paano, anong ginagawa niya, paano nagko-coordinate halimbawa sa Ombudsman, sa DOJ, o kaya sa Kongreso para ma-flag down.

asr-000899
02:15:10.020 --> 02:15:26.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, di ba dapat ang Kongreso, in the exercise of its oversight function, makita yun para hindi naaabot ng matagal, ma-flag down na rin yung programang yun na nagkaroon ng anomalya.

asr-000900
02:15:43.000 --> 02:16:06.980
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yung report po ng COA ay nabibigyan po ng kopya yung House of Representatives, annual reports. At saka yung mga kaso na umabot ng Ombudsman, the COA personnel or auditors,

asr-000901
02:16:06.980 --> 02:16:11.160
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: sila po yung stand as witness for the prosecution.

asr-000902
02:16:12.480 --> 02:16:19.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yung annual audit reports, kailan po yan sinusubite ng COA sa Kongreso?

asr-000903
02:16:19.260 --> 02:16:27.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Because, you know, in the past, I worked in the House of Representatives for more than three decades.

asr-000904
02:16:28.020 --> 02:16:29.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Dati po, automatic.

asr-000905
02:16:30.000 --> 02:16:36.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yan, pinapadala sa mga opisina. Kahit agency annual reports, accomplishment reports, meron.

asr-000906
02:16:37.400 --> 02:16:43.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Pero, itong mga recent, in the recent past, wala pong napapadala ang COA.

asr-000907
02:16:44.440 --> 02:16:47.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Hindi ko po alam kung saan ninyo sa Kongreso yung sinasubmit.

asr-000908
02:16:48.100 --> 02:16:53.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Usually, I check sa website, budget hearing na po, wala pa yung annual audit report.

asr-000909
02:16:53.960 --> 02:16:58.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I already mentioned this during the committee hearings, kasi ang sinasabi ko po, napakahalaga.

asr-000910
02:17:00.000 --> 02:17:08.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ang annual audit reports ng COA para matulungan nyo ang Kongreso sa pag-exercise ng oversight function

asr-000911
02:17:08.860 --> 02:17:15.300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: at para mabusisi ng gusto yung budget ng mga ahensya. Matutulungan nyo po kami.

asr-000912
02:17:15.300 --> 02:17:25.540
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Ang annual audit report dito sa Kongreso is within one month from June 30 to hanggang July.

asr-000913
02:17:26.700 --> 02:17:29.300
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: So, ang opisina na binibigyan,

asr-000914
02:17:30.000 --> 02:17:35.040
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: po, ng hard copy, ay ang opisina po ng Speaker of the House.

asr-000915
02:17:35.620 --> 02:17:37.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Madam Chair.

asr-000916
02:17:38.160 --> 02:17:39.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Last question na lamang po.

asr-000917
02:17:40.040 --> 02:17:42.640
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: [unclear], Committee on Appropriations Chair.

asr-000918
02:17:43.580 --> 02:17:44.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000919
02:17:45.300 --> 02:17:49.540
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Huling question na lamang po, on transparency naman po ito and accessibility.

asr-000920
02:17:50.340 --> 02:17:58.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Paano po natin nasisiguro na ang, yung mga audit reports din, ay madaling ma-access ng publiko?

asr-000921
02:17:58.000 --> 02:17:59.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kung ako nga po, medyo hirap.

asr-000922
02:18:00.000 --> 02:18:00.660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Nang konti.

asr-000923
02:18:00.980 --> 02:18:02.480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Paano pa po yung publiko?

asr-000924
02:18:02.600 --> 02:18:11.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Paano ito madaling ma-access ng publiko, ng civil society, para magsilbing dagdag na bantay laban sa korupsyon?

asr-000925
02:18:15.440 --> 02:18:23.100
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: For example, Madam, yung for year 25, example lang ito.

asr-000926
02:18:24.880 --> 02:18:29.680
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Ito po ay available sa COA website on October

asr-000927
02:18:30.000 --> 02:18:32.720
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: 31, 2026.

asr-000928
02:18:33.220 --> 02:18:34.260
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: So, ngayon, wala pa.

asr-000929
02:18:35.560 --> 02:18:38.100
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: October 31, 2026.

asr-000930
02:18:38.400 --> 02:18:40.060
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Andiyan na po yan sa COA website.

asr-000931
02:18:40.500 --> 02:18:48.780
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yung annual audit report ng COA sa current, yung previous year, 2025.

asr-000932
02:18:49.780 --> 02:18:51.120
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: So, yun po.

asr-000933
02:18:51.120 --> 02:18:58.480
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: I think mga 10 months, 10 months after sa previous year.

asr-000934
02:18:59.280 --> 02:18:59.980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you.

asr-000936
02:19:02.080 --> 02:19:06.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Siguro po, yun lamang ang aking mga katanungan.

asr-000937
02:19:06.540 --> 02:19:10.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Nais ko lang po sabihin sa huling na sa bawat pisong nasasayang sa korupsyon,

asr-000938
02:19:11.280 --> 02:19:14.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: isang Pilipino ang nawawalan ng servisyong dapat sa kanya.

asr-000939
02:19:15.040 --> 02:19:18.760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kung tunay nating nais nawakasan ang kultura ng katiwalian,

asr-000940
02:19:19.180 --> 02:19:22.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: dapat nating tiyakin na ang COA ay may sapat na lakas,

asr-000941
02:19:23.220 --> 02:19:29.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sapat na tao, at sapat na integridad upang bantayan ang bawat sentimo

asr-000942
02:19:29.080 --> 02:19:29.980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ng kaban ng bayan.

asr-000943
02:19:30.000 --> 02:19:36.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sa ganitong paraan natin, maipapakita sa sambayanan na ang gobyerno ay seryoso

asr-000944
02:19:36.620 --> 02:19:41.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: laban sa korupsyon at ang tiwala ng taong bayan ay tunay na mahalaga.

asr-000945
02:19:42.300 --> 02:19:46.580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po, Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor at sa COA po.

asr-000946
02:19:48.000 --> 02:19:48.960
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

asr-000947
02:19:51.000 --> 02:19:55.540
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Toby M. Tiangco

asr-000948
02:19:55.540 --> 02:19:59.980
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: of the Lone District of Navotas to interpellate on the proposed budget of the Commission on Audit.

asr-000949
02:20:00.000 --> 02:20:03.420
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Tiangco is recognized. Please proceed.

asr-000950
02:20:05.920 --> 02:20:10.220
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Madam Speaker, I commend po the job that the COA is doing

asr-000951
02:20:10.220 --> 02:20:16.140
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: para po masiguradong maayos po yung gastos ng pera ng ating mga kababayan.

asr-000952
02:20:16.660 --> 02:20:19.760
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So, ang unang tanong ko po is,

asr-000953
02:20:20.660 --> 02:20:25.420
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: ang audit po ng COA is based on the calendar year, no?

asr-000954
02:20:26.060 --> 02:20:29.000
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: The end of December 31 of every year. Tama po ba?

asr-000955
02:20:30.000 --> 02:20:32.060
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yes, sir.

asr-000956
02:20:34.160 --> 02:20:38.540
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kailan naman po ang deadline ng paglabas ng audit report?

asr-000957
02:20:39.480 --> 02:20:46.160
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: For example po, yung December 31, 2025, kailan po ang deadline ng paglabas ng audit report niya?

asr-000958
02:20:53.620 --> 02:20:58.120
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: To be specific, Distinguished Interpellator,

asr-000959
02:20:58.960 --> 02:20:59.920
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: yung sa...

asr-000960
02:20:59.920 --> 02:21:04.360
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: completion of audit report ng ahensya, June 30.

asr-000961
02:21:05.420 --> 02:21:08.140
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: So, at ito yung after June 30,

asr-000962
02:21:09.020 --> 02:21:12.540
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: ibigay po ito sa RAS, sa House,

asr-000963
02:21:13.260 --> 02:21:14.860
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Speaker, saka sa APRO.

asr-000964
02:21:15.620 --> 02:21:20.300
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Then, yung publication niya is October 31.

asr-000965
02:21:21.500 --> 02:21:26.180
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yun po ang petsa under the GAA, General Appropriation Act.

asr-000966
02:21:26.800 --> 02:21:29.840
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay. So, kaya po, as of now, wala pa po.

asr-000967
02:21:29.920 --> 02:21:32.300
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Hindi pa po napapublish ng COA

asr-000968
02:21:32.300 --> 02:21:35.680
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: yung audit report ng House of Representatives. Tama po ba?

asr-000969
02:21:36.380 --> 02:21:37.160
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Hindi pa po.

asr-000970
02:21:37.880 --> 02:21:39.300
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Pero meron ng kopya tayo.

asr-000971
02:21:39.640 --> 02:21:41.280
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: We have an advance copy.

asr-000972
02:21:41.580 --> 02:21:42.180
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yung House.

asr-000973
02:21:43.860 --> 02:21:44.300
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay.

asr-000974
02:21:45.820 --> 02:21:48.860
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Ngayon, dito po sa House of Representatives,

asr-000975
02:21:48.860 --> 02:21:50.220
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: ang congressman po,

asr-000976
02:21:51.120 --> 02:21:54.540
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: yung mga gastos po natin sa distrito,

asr-000977
02:21:55.320 --> 02:21:58.800
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: alam naman po natin yan is liquidation by certification po yan.

asr-000978
02:21:58.920 --> 02:21:59.380
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Tama po ba?

asr-000979
02:21:59.920 --> 02:22:03.320
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Yes, po.

asr-000980
02:22:04.020 --> 02:22:06.320
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: At yan po ay pinapayagan po ng COA.

asr-000981
02:22:06.720 --> 02:22:07.220
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Tama po.

asr-000982
02:22:11.260 --> 02:22:17.680
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Pursuant to COA Circular 89-300 of 1989,

asr-000983
02:22:18.660 --> 02:22:22.400
Rep. John Tracy F. Cagas: Ito po ang ginagamit na basihan at pinapayagan po.

asr-000984
02:22:25.820 --> 02:22:26.540
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Ngayon.

asr-000985
02:22:28.340 --> 02:22:29.540
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So, ang...

asr-000986
02:22:29.920 --> 02:22:31.440
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: M-O-O-E

asr-000987
02:22:31.440 --> 02:22:33.640
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: ng bawat congressman

