asr-004647
06:06:16.380 --> 06:06:19.700
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: are still at the freezing or preservation stage

asr-004648
06:06:19.700 --> 06:06:22.460
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: because the cases were filed only recently.

asr-004649
06:06:22.460 --> 06:06:25.900
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: In 2025, 15 of the 30 freeze orders,

asr-004650
06:06:25.900 --> 06:06:27.620
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: issued by the Court of Appeals,

asr-004651
06:06:27.620 --> 06:06:28.980
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: involve corruption,

asr-004652
06:06:28.980 --> 06:06:31.700
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: including 14 of the flood control anomalies,

asr-004653
06:06:31.700 --> 06:06:36.540
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: covering 20.26 billion.

asr-004654
06:06:36.540 --> 06:06:39.180
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: In the first semester of 2026,

asr-004655
06:06:39.180 --> 06:06:42.580
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: 18 of the 28 petitions for civil forfeiture

asr-004656
06:06:42.580 --> 06:06:44.780
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: filed were corruption cases,

asr-004657
06:06:44.780 --> 06:06:48.460
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: covering 15.76 billion in preserved assets.

asr-004658
06:06:48.460 --> 06:06:52.740
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: 57% of all assets preserved during the period.

asr-004659
06:06:52.740 --> 06:06:54.500
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: As of June 30, 2026, five active cases,

asr-004660
06:06:54.500 --> 06:06:55.220
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: including the one that was filed,

asr-004661
06:06:55.220 --> 06:06:58.300
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: five active freeze orders in corruption cases,

asr-004662
06:06:58.300 --> 06:07:01.420
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: over another 1.01 billion.

asr-004663
06:07:01.420 --> 06:07:04.700
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: These cases are pending before the RTC

asr-004664
06:07:04.700 --> 06:07:07.900
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: and judgment of forfeiture will follow trial.

asr-004665
06:07:07.900 --> 06:07:12.860
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: The flood control cases alone accounted for 22 petitions,

asr-004666
06:07:12.860 --> 06:07:16.100
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: covering about 16 billion in preserved assets,

asr-004667
06:07:16.100 --> 06:07:19.260
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: as of September 16, 2026.

asr-004668
06:07:19.260 --> 06:07:22.980
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Across all of its cases since 2006,

asr-004669
06:07:22.980 --> 06:07:24.940
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: the courts have issued 106 forfeiture cases,

asr-004670
06:07:24.940 --> 06:07:29.100
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: forfeiture orders covering 2.17 billion.

asr-004671
06:07:29.100 --> 06:07:33.500
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Of these, 774 million has been returned to victims,

asr-004672
06:07:33.500 --> 06:07:37.460
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: 166 million has been turned over to the national government,

asr-004673
06:07:37.460 --> 06:07:39.860
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: and 119 million has been transferred

asr-004674
06:07:39.860 --> 06:07:41.940
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: to the Office of the Ombudsman,

asr-004675
06:07:41.940 --> 06:07:45.780
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: while the balance is still at various stages of execution.

asr-004676
06:07:45.780 --> 06:07:46.900
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: Mr. Speaker.

asr-004677
06:07:46.900 --> 06:07:51.420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mrs. Speaker, Madam Sponsor.

asr-004678
06:07:51.420 --> 06:07:53.780
