asr-004688
06:08:22.180 --> 06:08:24.900
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: or another agency already identifies us,

asr-004689
06:08:24.900 --> 06:08:29.220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: we recognize that we are a suspect and AMLOC then traces the person's account.

asr-004690
06:08:29.220 --> 06:08:30.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That is important work.

asr-004691
06:08:30.740 --> 06:08:32.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: We recognize that.

asr-004692
06:08:32.060 --> 06:08:37.820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But AMLOC also received enormous amounts of financial information

asr-004693
06:08:37.820 --> 06:08:41.140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: from banks and other covered persons.

asr-004694
06:08:41.140 --> 06:08:47.660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So AMLOC should also be capable of identifying suspicious financial activity

asr-004695
06:08:47.660 --> 06:08:52.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: on their own and investigation based on the information.

asr-004696
06:08:52.300 --> 06:08:54.220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How often does that happen?

asr-004697
06:08:54.900 --> 06:08:58.220
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: It happens regularly and increasingly.

asr-004698
06:08:58.220 --> 06:09:04.100
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: In the first semester of 2026, 751 of the AMLOCs,

asr-004699
06:09:04.100 --> 06:09:10.020
Rep. Ma. Isabel L. Sagarbarria: 1,165 financial intelligence products were generated on its own initiative,

asr-004700
06:09:10.020 --> 06:09:13.420
